 correct diagram is shown below: \n\n![](images/1a/1a704d0dd679fa71874b7485173ae83d35892dba6018e170f83aa9e119bcc315.png)" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186114986 #edb/ref 1069 "e-2730" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186114986 #edb/ref 1071 "Consider the triangle $ABC$ shown below. Construct the height corresponding to $\\overline{BC}.$\n\n![](images/72/72b40526cafc5d1db902ea9947a2808020dfadcf6a84238e8e3a2459ca95fe07.png)" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186114986 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "2e6213d0-702f-5795-a99a-0051790c4e6d" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186114986 #edb/ref 1074 "The height (or altitude) corresponding to $\\overline{BC}$ is a line segment that \n\n- runs from the opposite vertex $A$ to the line $\\overset{\\longleftrightarrow}{BC},$ and\n\n- is perpendicular to $\\overset{\\longleftrightarrow}{BC}.$\n\nTo draw the height, we proceed as follows:\n\n- Extend the line segment $\\overline{BC}.$\n\n![](images/01/010d2c4de6c3df93112295eb2351247c2162a0d84a1f6e122fdca71dca72c168.png)\n\n- Draw the perpendicular from $A$ to $\\overset{\\longleftrightarrow}{BC}.$\n\n![](images/39/392d7d23590557ccce29b25cecabb276ee875f86c172ce15c845c13668939933.png)" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186115160 #edb/ref 1069 "e-9731" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186115160 #edb/ref 1071 "![](images/33/33700b49845ba054447ce69356324d3e421d256344149b447756cdbf0cf5a905.png)\n\nConsider $\\triangle ABC$ shown above. The line segment $\\overline{CH}$ is the altitude corresponding to $\\overline{AB}.$ If $m\\angle BAC = 115^\\circ,$ calculate $m\\angle HCA.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186115160 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "43c770ec-d353-5e9e-b44e-f06417dab2ab" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186115160 #edb/ref 1074 "Since the straight angle must have a measure of $180^\\circ,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}m∠HAC+m∠BAC & ={180}^{∘} \\\\ m∠HAC+{115}^{∘} & ={180}^{∘} \\\\ m∠HAC & ={65}^{∘}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNote that $\\triangle ACH$ is a right triangle. Since its interior angles must sum to $180^\\circ,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}m∠HCA+m∠HAC+m∠AHC & ={180}^{∘} \\\\ m∠HCA+{65}^{∘}+{90}^{∘} & ={180}^{∘} \\\\ m∠HCA+{155}^{∘} & ={180}^{∘} \\\\ m∠HCA & ={25}^{∘}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186115336 #edb/ref 1037 #edb/ref 17592186048723 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186115336 #edb/ref 1037 #edb/ref 17592186049949 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186115336 #edb/ref 1037 #edb/ref 17592186050410 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186115336 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186115491 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186115336 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186115655 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186115336 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186253502 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186115336 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186253503 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186115336 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186269004 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186115336 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186294980 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186115336 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186500347 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186115336 #edb/ref 1039 "Calculating an Unknown Angle" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186115336 #edb/ref 1041 #edb/ref 17592186115160 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186115336 #edb/ref 1042 #uuid "6a916099-a237-5612-b7f1-3679b7ff069d" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186115409 #edb/ref 1037 #edb/ref 17592186050357 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186115409 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186115646 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186115409 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186115952 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186115409 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186253495 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186115409 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186253496 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186115409 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186294864 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186115409 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186386882 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186115409 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186393737 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186115409 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186500371 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [1759218611540